<http://data.silknow.org/object/0b396fd5-9883-37e9-8a8c-7eb4bf98a21b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Brocaded silk and metal thread.\nThe border is dominated by a band of four 8-pointed stars, each made of outward facing floral motifs. There are six half-stars and four quarter stars in the corners. Between these are large X-motifs which create a disjointed diamond shaped grid on the red/pink ground. The X-motifs are woven with a chequered pattern using metal thread. \nMetal Thread: silver strip open S-wound on a white silk core. One of the stars is woven completely with dark blue silk; the others have half their pattern woven with beige silk.\nThere are other irregularities in the colouring with a light blue band at the bottom of the main panel changed to darker blue.\nThe border is woven in red/pink silk and metal thread with a bold pattern of pairs of silver split palmettes, alternately inward and outward facing on a red/pink ground. There is a very narrow band of reciprocal brown and silver trefoils.\nMaterials and Techniques: silk thread, metal thread, weaving"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0b396fd5-9883-37e9-8a8c-7eb4bf98a21b> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/0b396fd5-9883-37e9-8a8c-7eb4bf98a21b>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Middle East, Textile; woven silk, 1700s, Persian"@en , "Brocaded silk and metal thread.\nThe border is dominated by a band of four 8-pointed stars, each made of outward facing floral motifs. There are six half-stars and four quarter stars in the corners. Between these are large X-motifs which create a disjointed diamond shaped grid on the red/pink ground. The X-motifs are woven with a chequered pattern using metal thread. \nMetal Thread: silver strip open S-wound on a white silk core. One of the stars is woven completely with dark blue silk; the others have half their pattern woven with beige silk.\nThere are other irregularities in the colouring with a light blue band at the bottom of the main panel changed to darker blue.\nThe border is woven in red/pink silk and metal thread with a bold pattern of pairs of silver split palmettes, alternately inward and outward facing on a red/pink ground. There is a very narrow band of reciprocal brown and silver trefoils.\nMaterials and Techniques: silk thread, metal thread, weaving"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/7acd7309-17c4-316a-9260-642bc1289661> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/695dcb26-a4bc-3f31-8e67-d0ef2c8d1741> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/4dfd32ea-050f-3f83-bbd4-e44a5acf8069> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/49a9a900-cefa-37fe-9b09-1e16f5de0b9b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Brocaded silk and metal thread.\nThe border is dominated by a band of four 8-pointed stars, each made of outward facing floral motifs. There are six half-stars and four quarter stars in the corners. Between these are large X-motifs which create a disjointed diamond shaped grid on the red/pink ground. The X-motifs are woven with a chequered pattern using metal thread. \nMetal Thread: silver strip open S-wound on a white silk core. One of the stars is woven completely with dark blue silk; the others have half their pattern woven with beige silk.\nThere are other irregularities in the colouring with a light blue band at the bottom of the main panel changed to darker blue.\nThe border is woven in red/pink silk and metal thread with a bold pattern of pairs of silver split palmettes, alternately inward and outward facing on a red/pink ground. There is a very narrow band of reciprocal brown and silver trefoils.\nMaterials and Techniques: silk thread, metal thread, weaving"@en , "Middle East, Textile; woven silk, 1700s, Persian"@en ;
